{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>All my plagues.</b> Rashi explained: we learn from here that the plague of the firstborn is equivalent, etc. — these are the plants of the earth and the trees that hastened to bud early, and the hail struck them. Another interpretation: <b>all my plagues</b> — many kinds of afflictions: fire and hail, stones of alabaster, sulfur, snow, steam." "<b>[All my plagues.</b> Many of His plagues.]" "<b>El levavkha.</b> For even a person's heart is broken within him out of great fear. אל לבך — the bet has a shuruk (as לְבָבְךָ, full plural form)."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:42.905431166Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}